                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Who would have thought that in apocalyptic pandas will rule the world, fighting an army of hogs, would make a so amusing gameplay experience? \nIt was inevitable that at some point, someone in this big world that we live in will create a so fascinating future.\n\nThe, game developed by \"[b]Skandivania Games[/b]\", falls in an indie, rouge-lite category, that is wonderful complemented by a little of 2D gore elements, and it feels like your typical top-down action shooter with some Binding of Isaac influence.\n\nAs you might except, from a top-down shooter, the plot is simple, but all you need to know is that you are panda, equipped with various guns and weapons who needs to kill whatever you can, make your way trough the rooms and find the key to escape each level. Everything seems simple so far, but the're a catch; all the levels and loot are randomized, alongside the other main thing: every death is permanent. \n\nThe story mode challenges you to make your way trough the randomly generated levels, grouped into five chapters. With a little luck and if you manage to always be ready and think quickly you will manage to see the end of the game.\n\nEach stage is made up of a number of interconnected rooms and your main goal is to retrieve a keycard and make your way to the exit. Alongside the main rooms, there are a lot of secrets hidden behind destructible walls, lots of items from the crates, or just buy the items you need from merchants and vending machines. In your journey you may encounter rooms with no enemies, so you shall breath freely and enjoy one of the few safe moments you will encounter, as most of the rooms are full of enemies and traps.\n\nYou must develop skills to be able survive, and you can't afford to idle when danger is close.\n\nThe graphics and art style don’t do a ton to stand out, but they work fine for this type of game. \n\n[b]Pros:[/b][quote] \n> Fun action. \n> Decent effects and graphics. \n> Random generated maps and loot. \n> One play through leads to another. \n[/quote] \n[b]Cons:[/b] [quote] \n> Same enemies everywhere. \n> Too few room templates. \n[/quote] \nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=BzlC3A_8YBw",
